{"name":"Midnight Sonata","hex":"#225374","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"},{"term":"sonata","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical composition for one or a few instruments, one of which is frequently a piano, in three or four movements that vary in key and tempo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sonata"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight is the transition time from one day to the next – the moment when the date changes, on the local official clock time for any particular jurisdiction. By clock time, midnight is the opposite of noon, differing from it by 12 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight","wikidata":"Q36402"},{"title":"Sonata","blocks":[{"text":"In music, a sonata is a piece that consists of 3 or 4 movements that can be for different musical instruments. The term evolved through the history of music, designating a variety of forms until the Classical era, when it took on increasing importance. Sonata is a vague term, with varying meanings depending on the context and time period. By the early 19th century it came to represent a principle of composing large-scale works. It was applied to most instrumental genres and regarded—alongside the fugue—as one of two fundamental methods of organizing, interpreting and analyzing concert music. Though the musical style of sonatas has changed since the Classical era, most 20th- and 21st-century sonatas maintain the overarching structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Beethoven_opus_101_manuscript.jpg/330px-Beethoven_opus_101_manuscript.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonata","wikidata":"Q131269"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of the moon taken at midnight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidnight_Mist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Archive-ugent-be-0B4371EA-DD2B-11E1-8693-E85B8375B242_DS-5_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Archive-ugent-be-0B4371EA-DD2B-11E1-8693-E85B8375B242_DS-5_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Archive-ugent-be-0B4371EA-DD2B-11E1-8693-E85B8375B242_D